546
00:54:51.333 --> 00:54:53.385
You go in knowing how to get out.

547
00:54:53.546 --> 00:54:55.349
By the way, how'd you get in?

548
00:54:57.053 --> 00:54:59.438
- Prison's easy to get in.
- Open Door 16.

549
00:54:59.600 --> 00:55:01.486
Getting out's the hard pan.

550
00:55:11.332 --> 00:55:12.340
You're on form.

551
00:55:12.543 --> 00:55:13.717
Yeah, I guess.

552
00:55:14.880 --> 00:55:16.091
Let's take a short cut.

553
00:55:24.065 --> 00:55:25.239
That's your short cut?

554
00:55:54.043 --> 00:55:55.596
Damien's escaped.

555
00:55:56.005 --> 00:55:57.761
He got out of the building?

556
00:55:58.093 --> 00:55:59.730
Apparently he's still inside.

557
00:56:00.097 --> 00:56:01.224
Find him.

558
00:56:01.976 --> 00:56:02.770
Fast!

559
00:56:02.936 --> 00:56:06.068
In the last 24 hours,
riots have erupted in D13.

560
00:56:06.234 --> 00:56:06.863
Gentlemen.

561
00:56:08.864 --> 00:56:10.074
It's started?

562
00:56:10.701 --> 00:56:13.999
A gang destroyed the police station
with a bazooka.

563
00:56:14.167 --> 00:56:16.338
Since then,
fighting has intensified.

564
00:56:16.546 --> 00:56:19.050
Many officers have been wounded.

565
00:56:19.219 --> 00:56:21.722
As we speak, the rioting continues.

566
00:56:21.890 --> 00:56:24.144
Commissioner? Latest news?

567
00:56:24.771 --> 00:56:26.741
D13 is out of control.

568
00:56:26.900 --> 00:56:30.412
In the next few hours,
other districts will blow up.

569
00:56:30.700 --> 00:56:33.168
Unless we act, it'll be civil war.

570
00:56:33.873 --> 00:56:34.585
General?

571
00:56:36.043 --> 00:56:38.428
Is a pre-emptive
military strike possible?

572
00:56:38.591 --> 00:56:40.263
Yes, but they're well armed.

573
00:56:40.427 --> 00:56:43.061
Without time to prepare,
we face heavy losses.

574
00:56:44.185 --> 00:56:47.447
Unfortunately,
time is a luxury we don't have.

575
00:56:50.197 --> 00:56:52.534
Mr Gassman,
what do you recommend?

576
00:56:54.080 --> 00:56:56.417
When the gangrene spreads,
amputate.

577
00:56:56.584 --> 00:56:57.712
Shit!

578
00:56:58.005 --> 00:57:02.893
I didn't leave the G10 summit
to hear medical clichés like that.

579
00:57:03.056 --> 00:57:05.358
I asked what you recommend.

580
00:57:05.561 --> 00:57:07.648
Fine, I'll be more direct.

581
00:57:07.940 --> 00:57:09.862
We evacuate D13 in 12 hours.

582
00:57:10.029 --> 00:57:13.623
We blow up the five high-rises
awash with arms and drugs.

583
00:57:13.786 --> 00:57:15.506
That calms the others.

584
00:57:16.125 --> 00:57:17.465
It creates jobs.

585
00:57:17.627 --> 00:57:20.391
We rebuild a neighbourhood
for the middle classes,

586
00:57:20.717 --> 00:57:22.603
who'll vote for you next time.

587
00:57:25.894 --> 00:57:27.899
That's honest, at least.

588
00:57:28.566 --> 00:57:29.574
Gentlemen?

589
00:57:31.112 --> 00:57:33.034
What do you say to that?

590
00:57:33.785 --> 00:57:36.253
Politically, it's very extreme.

591
00:57:36.791 --> 00:57:38.001
A better idea?

592
00:57:44.640 --> 00:57:45.767
Fine.

593
00:57:46.393 --> 00:57:49.905
I see nobody can think
of a way to defend

594
00:57:50.192 --> 00:57:52.447
our democracy. That's interesting.

595
00:57:52.990 --> 00:57:57.047
Remember, we're here to protect
the people and their interests,

596
00:57:57.207 --> 00:58:01.264
and to make sure our values
of liberty, equality and fraternity

597
00:58:01.590 --> 00:58:03.512
are respected in this country.

598
00:58:03.678 --> 00:58:08.352
It's what you might call
the bottom line of our Republic.

599
00:58:09.064 --> 00:58:12.825
Your proposal is to walk
all over ii. ls that the idea?

600
00:58:13.448 --> 00:58:14.124
Thank you.

601
00:58:14.575 --> 00:58:19.130
My idea's detestable
and against our fundamental values,

602
00:58:19.710 --> 00:58:21.881
but what else can we do in 12 hours

603
00:58:22.048 --> 00:58:24.682
before the situation
becomes unmanageable?

604
00:58:24.845 --> 00:58:29.401
It may not be the best idea,
but it's far from the worst.

605
00:58:29.814 --> 00:58:30.857
General...

606
00:58:31.901 --> 00:58:34.618
Can we evacuate one million
in 12 hours?

607
00:58:35.157 --> 00:58:37.293
If you say so now, it's possible.

608
00:58:37.496 --> 00:58:41.257
Some of these warlords
won't evacuate without a fight.

609
00:58:41.504 --> 00:58:42.596
Who'll mourn them?

610
00:58:55.950 --> 00:58:56.579
General...

611
00:58:58.454 --> 00:59:00.257
Proceed with evacuation.

612
00:59:00.709 --> 00:59:05.050
We'll decide tomorrow if we should
demolish the high-rises.

613
00:59:06.304 --> 00:59:07.312
Mr Gassman...

614
00:59:08.016 --> 00:59:12.406
I demand that all inhabitants
be treated with respect and dignity.

615
00:59:12.566 --> 00:59:14.618
And I mean all of them.

616
00:59:15.113 --> 00:59:17.581
I'll see to it personally.

617
00:59:18.703 --> 00:59:19.665
You can go.

618
00:59:31.479 --> 00:59:32.607
Look behind you.

619
00:59:43.294 --> 00:59:44.967
Lei's wait till it calms down.

620
00:59:47.971 --> 00:59:50.106
Why were you in jail, super-cop?

621
00:59:50.852 --> 00:59:53.071
Three kilos of heroin in my kitchen.

622
00:59:53.398 --> 00:59:54.786
That's very careless.

623
00:59:54.943 --> 00:59:55.821
Ii wasn't mine.

624
00:59:55.987 --> 00:59:59.333
The cops planted it there,
Standard procedure.

625
00:59:59.745 --> 01:00:01.916
Cops setting up a cop?
That's new.

626
01:00:02.082 --> 01:00:03.506
Yes, and I wonder why.

627
01:00:03.920 --> 01:00:05.972
To stop you snooping somewhere.

628
01:00:06.216 --> 01:00:07.888
- It's your specialty.
- Explain.

629
01:00:08.053 --> 01:00:10.936
When your corrupt government
plans a low blow,

630
01:00:11.101 --> 01:00:12.987
they get rid of honest cops.

631
01:00:13.940 --> 01:00:16.027
They could have given me leave.

632
01:00:16.153 --> 01:00:18.074
In a crisis,
you'd stay on leave?

633
01:00:19.659 --> 01:00:20.833
No, I guess not.

634
01:00:25.963 --> 01:00:27.434
Maybe it's linked.

635
01:00:28.427 --> 01:00:29.305
To what?

636
01:00:29.513 --> 01:00:33.653
Film number one shows a cop car
being shot up in D13.

637
01:00:35.316 --> 01:00:37.535
Film number two shows ii two hours earlier.

638
01:00:37.988 --> 01:00:41.202
Four cops shot by undercover guys,
the car in a truck...

639
01:00:41.370 --> 01:00:42.711
And dumped in D13.

640
01:00:43.875 --> 01:00:45.465
You're as sharp as ever.

641
01:00:45.628 --> 01:00:46.506
And then?

642
01:00:46.756 --> 01:00:49.092
Light the powder keg, it explodes.

643
01:00:50.680 --> 01:00:53.610
I got your message
and men in black swarmed in.

644
01:00:53.770 --> 01:00:55.656
The guys that killed the cops.

645
01:00:56.233 --> 01:00:58.238
The guys that took the car...

646
01:00:58.780 --> 01:01:01.200
And took Samir who filmed it all.

647
01:01:01.451 --> 01:01:03.207
- Who says they're cops?
- Please!

648
01:01:03.372 --> 01:01:05.092
Could be a disguise.

649
01:01:05.752 --> 01:01:07.722
What for? Fun?

650
01:01:08.257 --> 01:01:10.891
No, only cops
benefit from D13 blowing up.

651
01:01:11.054 --> 01:01:12.976
Gives 'em an excuse to clean up.

652
01:01:13.142 --> 01:01:15.112
So they got me out of the way?

653
01:01:15.271 --> 01:01:16.232
Logical.

654
01:01:19.196 --> 01:01:21.580
What were the men in black driving?

655
01:01:21.784 --> 01:01:25.414
Big SUVs. Black, armor-plated.
Same plates. DISS.

656
01:01:28.840 --> 01:01:31.473
- DISS? No way!
- What's DISS?

657
01:01:33.141 --> 01:01:34.980
Department of Internal State Security.

658
01:01:35.729 --> 01:01:36.607
Sexy!

659
01:01:36.814 --> 01:01:38.487
They report to no one.

660
01:01:38.943 --> 01:01:41.661
Except a five-star general
and the president.

661
01:01:41.866 --> 01:01:44.666
They're run
by a guy called Walter Gassman.

662
01:01:44.789 --> 01:01:46.176
Friend of yours?

663
01:01:46.334 --> 01:01:47.675
Not really.

664
01:01:48.170 --> 01:01:50.471
He offered me a job.
I refused.

665
01:01:51.009 --> 01:01:54.521
Thais it. We have the motive,
crime and criminal.

666
01:01:56.270 --> 01:01:57.563
Now we need proof.

667
01:01:59.736 --> 01:02:00.697
Here...

668
01:02:06.499 --> 01:02:08.005
Your video's not enough.

669
01:02:09.254 --> 01:02:11.176
We need proof Gassman's involved.

670
01:02:18.356 --> 01:02:19.993
- What are you doing?
- Thinking.

671
01:02:20.485 --> 01:02:22.325
I don't like it when you think.

672
01:02:23.033 --> 01:02:24.835
We'll go to Walter's office.

673
01:02:25.078 --> 01:02:27.463
I knew ii! Where is it?

674
01:02:27.833 --> 01:02:29.304
First floor. Room 'I 17.

675
01:02:32.176 --> 01:02:33.813
Just like old times?

676
01:02:34.555 --> 01:02:36.145
OK, old times.

677
01:02:57.769 --> 01:02:59.525
Isn't this a bit conspicuous?

678
01:03:00.315 --> 01:03:01.905
More people, less conspicuous.

679
01:03:06.077 --> 01:03:07.169
Now what do we do?

680
01:03:08.331 --> 01:03:09.802
Let me think.

681
01:03:10.879 --> 01:03:12.599
- There!
- You think too much.

682
01:03:41.815 --> 01:03:43.571
Got an idea? No thinking.

683
01:03:44.404 --> 01:03:46.705
I'll distract 'em.
You play Spider-Man.

684
01:03:46.867 --> 01:03:48.587
His office is Room 117.

685
01:03:48.746 --> 01:03:51.131
Grab anything we can use as proof.

686
01:03:51.293 --> 01:03:52.504
Where do we meet?

687
01:03:53.965 --> 01:03:56.266
I won't be going very far.
Move it!

688
01:04:53.710 --> 01:04:55.929
Just sit there and you'll be fine.

689
01:04:56.256 --> 01:04:57.644
You have my word.

690
01:05:00.807 --> 01:05:02.777
Where are his personal files?

691
01:05:06.401 --> 01:05:07.529
Have you got the code?

692
01:05:19.428 --> 01:05:22.227
Anyone's computer
just go for a walk?

693
01:05:22.642 --> 01:05:23.604
Yes, mine.

694
01:05:24.646 --> 01:05:27.861
Technical support.
I'll install your new server.

695
01:05:30.659 --> 01:05:32.711
But first we lose the old one.

696
01:05:37.339 --> 01:05:38.680
Found ii.

697
01:05:43.727 --> 01:05:44.770
Thanks, guys.

698
01:06:26.271 --> 01:06:31.194
Just lie down and let the judges
solve your problems, not your fists.

699
01:06:34.537 --> 01:06:35.415
Roland,

700
01:06:35.706 --> 01:06:37.296
you know I'm innocent.

701
01:06:38.086 --> 01:06:39.379
Yeah, I know.

702
01:06:39.839 --> 01:06:41.725
Jails are full of innocent men.

703
01:06:43.639 --> 01:06:45.311
Lie down and shut up.

704
01:06:48.022 --> 01:06:49.280
Let's go.

705
01:07:06.267 --> 01:07:07.478
Don't you like doors?

706
01:07:07.646 --> 01:07:09.651
They slow you down.
Find anything?

707
01:07:09.817 --> 01:07:11.157
- A hard drive.
- Cool.

708
01:07:11.529 --> 01:07:12.703
Don't let them out!

709
01:07:16.037 --> 01:07:16.915
Shit!

710
01:07:19.127 --> 01:07:20.515
Maybe we should walk?

711
01:07:20.672 --> 01:07:21.764
Belt up!

712
01:07:43.217 --> 01:07:45.898
- That's his office.
- I know. Let's renovate.

713
01:08:03.883 --> 01:08:04.726
Excuse me.

714
01:08:10.397 --> 01:08:12.532
- Damien escaped.
- How?

715
01:08:12.693 --> 01:08:15.161
Leito came for him.
They got away.

716
01:08:15.449 --> 01:08:17.454
How'd they get out of HQ?

717
01:08:19.414 --> 01:08:20.588
Through your office.

718
01:08:21.544 --> 01:08:23.347
We call ii off?
Cover our tracks?

719
01:08:23.506 --> 01:08:26.186
Too late.
The military's moving in.

720
01:08:26.345 --> 01:08:27.686
We'll cover up later.

721
01:08:27.848 --> 01:08:30.269
In the meantime,
find them and kill them, OK?

722
01:08:30.395 --> 01:08:31.356
Got it.

723
01:08:36.867 --> 01:08:39.547
Follow the instructions
you were given.

724
01:08:48.306 --> 01:08:50.145
Where are you taking us?

725
01:08:50.310 --> 01:08:51.698
Where?

726
01:09:21.748 --> 01:09:23.421
A warm welcome as always.

727
01:09:23.752 --> 01:09:27.715
Didn't you promise change?
Because idiots enforce the law.

728
01:09:27.969 --> 01:09:30.354
Blame the guys who oversee the law.

729
01:09:30.767 --> 01:09:33.531
Li's like religion.
What are you?

730
01:09:34.231 --> 01:09:37.494
I was baptized, but my bible
now is the Constitution.

731
01:09:38.950 --> 01:09:39.709
What?

732
01:09:40.035 --> 01:09:41.589
"My bible's the Constitution"?

733
01:09:41.956 --> 01:09:44.459
Lucky you didn't read cookbooks
as a kid.

734
01:09:47.675 --> 01:09:49.727
- We moving or yakking?
- Moving.

735
01:10:11.515 --> 01:10:13.271
- What do you want?
- To see Tao.

736
01:10:13.644 --> 01:10:14.688
What about?

737
01:10:14.896 --> 01:10:16.984
Saving D13 and two million people.

738
01:10:18.111 --> 01:10:20.911
He's joking.
We've got a business proposal.

739
01:10:35.479 --> 01:10:36.737
Let them through.

740
01:10:57.107 --> 01:10:59.159
This isn't a flea market.

741
01:11:00.572 --> 01:11:02.742
We stole it
from a secret service honcho.

742
01:11:02.909 --> 01:11:05.460
It's all his confidential files.

743
01:11:06.208 --> 01:11:07.419
How much?

744
01:11:08.421 --> 01:11:10.224
It's free.
After we access

745
01:11:10.550 --> 01:11:11.891
the information we want.

746
01:11:12.053 --> 01:11:13.180
Who's Doofus?

747
01:11:13.473 --> 01:11:15.145
We met at Sunday school.

748
01:11:16.186 --> 01:11:18.820
You noticed they're evacuating D13?

749
01:11:19.150 --> 01:11:20.621
Then they'll destroy it.

750
01:11:20.821 --> 01:11:23.075
Doofus needs proof
so he can stop it.

751
01:11:27.626 --> 01:11:30.130
Manuel?
Make it talk.

752
01:11:57.979 --> 01:11:59.106
It's all yours.

753
01:11:59.273 --> 01:12:00.317
All of it?

754
01:12:00.484 --> 01:12:01.196
All of it.

755
01:12:01.527 --> 01:12:03.532
Where'd you learn your stuff?

756
01:12:03.865 --> 01:12:05.076
From manuals.

757
01:12:07.915 --> 01:12:09.671
Explains his name.
Get to work.

758
01:12:13.885 --> 01:12:16.056
Anything about China, I'll take.

759
01:12:16.474 --> 01:12:17.815
Iran for now.

760
01:12:18.102 --> 01:12:19.395
I'll take that, too.

761
01:12:19.814 --> 01:12:20.739
D13!

762
01:12:21.985 --> 01:12:25.034
The targets! Five high-rises.
And the contractor.

763
01:12:26.661 --> 01:12:28.002
Walter stirs up shit.

764
01:12:28.164 --> 01:12:30.714
The president demolishes,
Harriburton rebuilds.

765
01:12:31.087 --> 01:12:32.261
Like in Iraq.

766
01:12:32.422 --> 01:12:33.384
Yeah...

767
01:12:34.009 --> 01:12:35.730
Except they're French.

768
01:12:36.472 --> 01:12:38.145
How will they flatten the high-rises?

769
01:12:40.480 --> 01:12:41.691
Target zone in sight.

770
01:13:09.414 --> 01:13:12.048
Three choppers. One just overhead.

771
01:13:13.839 --> 01:13:16.687
Laser markers to guide the missiles.

772
01:13:22.565 --> 01:13:23.574
Fired when?

773
01:13:24.026 --> 01:13:25.948
Tomorrow morning from Army Command.

774
01:13:26.239 --> 01:13:28.540
Only the president
can give the order.

775
01:13:29.161 --> 01:13:30.419
How do we stop him?

776
01:13:30.582 --> 01:13:32.302
Check in the manual.

777
01:13:32.586 --> 01:13:35.089
Doofus is starting to feel tired.

778
01:13:37.303 --> 01:13:39.142
You don't like ”Doofus"?

779
01:13:42.396 --> 01:13:43.523
Sorry.

780
01:13:45.402 --> 01:13:47.573
What if I call you Cutie-pie?

781
01:13:47.866 --> 01:13:49.373
How about my name?

782
01:13:51.707 --> 01:13:52.632
What is it?

783
01:13:53.419 --> 01:13:56.930
Damien Tomasso,
Captain of French Elite Commandos.

784
01:13:57.803 --> 01:13:59.191
A cop, if you prefer.

785
01:14:02.479 --> 01:14:04.982
If we're a team,
forget your prejudices...

786
01:14:06.528 --> 01:14:08.165
and shake my hand.

787
01:14:20.306 --> 01:14:20.935
Tao.

788
01:14:21.726 --> 01:14:22.983
Nice to meet you.

789
01:14:23.313 --> 01:14:24.190
Same here.

790
01:14:27.571 --> 01:14:29.956
So what's the plan, Cutie-pie?

791
01:14:54.792 --> 01:14:57.094
- Thanks for coming.
- What's up?

792
01:14:57.631 --> 01:14:58.758
We'll explain.

793
01:15:18.048 --> 01:15:19.009
Hey...

794
01:15:21.011 --> 01:15:21.640
This way.

795
01:15:39.214 --> 01:15:40.223
Ali-K...

796
01:15:40.383 --> 01:15:42.637
A slender natural born killer.

797
01:15:43.097 --> 01:15:44.022
Molko...

798
01:15:45.018 --> 01:15:46.857
Specialist with a machete.

799
01:15:47.774 --> 01:15:49.162
Karl the Skinhead...

800
01:15:49.318 --> 01:15:51.619
Saw him smash up a car
with his head.

801
01:15:52.407 --> 01:15:53.535
Little Montana...

802
01:15:53.702 --> 01:15:56.039
Got a gun
where his heart should be.

803
01:15:56.667 --> 01:15:57.877
Sorry.

804
01:15:58.461 --> 01:15:59.719
Running late.

805
01:16:01.467 --> 01:16:02.939
Nice class reunion.

806
01:16:03.096 --> 01:16:03.939
Yeah.

807
01:16:04.390 --> 01:16:06.063
Let's take a photo.

808
01:16:12.991 --> 01:16:13.999
Guys...

809
01:16:15.204 --> 01:16:16.794
Thanks for coming.

810
01:16:18.252 --> 01:16:20.506
Since 7 PM,
D13 has been evacuated.

811
01:16:22.260 --> 01:16:24.146
They plan to blow it up tomorrow.

812
01:16:24.639 --> 01:16:25.980
If they need ordnance...

813
01:16:27.729 --> 01:16:30.576
The idea is to join forces
to prevent it.

814
01:16:32.906 --> 01:16:34.080
Who's for?

815
01:16:47.101 --> 01:16:48.607
Over to...

816
01:16:49.565 --> 01:16:51.404
Damien, who has a plan.

817
01:16:59.042 --> 01:17:01.462
First,
we evacuate anyone thats left.

818
01:17:01.714 --> 01:17:03.517
In the five hours we have left.

819
01:17:04.344 --> 01:17:08.140
Then I need 30
of your best fighters. But no guns.

820
01:17:08.310 --> 01:17:09.698
We're not on a hum.

821
01:17:10.564 --> 01:17:12.700
We sneak in, neutralize...

822
01:17:13.445 --> 01:17:14.833
and take the operations room.

823
01:17:17.871 --> 01:17:18.962
Any questions?

824
01:17:20.126 --> 01:17:21.597
Where's the party?

825
01:17:25.887 --> 01:17:27.643
There.
Downtown Paris.

826
01:17:42.421 --> 01:17:44.307
Mr President.

827
01:17:53.150 --> 01:17:54.906
Reinforce security.

828
01:17:58.620 --> 01:18:00.257
Tell Molko to be ready.

829
01:18:08.681 --> 01:18:10.686
Over the target
in under two minutes.

830
01:18:14.819 --> 01:18:16.207
Morning, gentlemen.

831
01:18:16.697 --> 01:18:17.705
Be seated.

832
01:18:19.495 --> 01:18:21.416
General? Status report.

833
01:18:21.582 --> 01:18:24.596
Two Jaguars await your order,
50 miles from target.

834
01:18:24.755 --> 01:18:27.768
I meant the evacuation,
not the demolition.

835
01:18:28.722 --> 01:18:30.691
Isn't that the right order?

836
01:18:30.976 --> 01:18:32.068
My apologies.

837
01:18:34.984 --> 01:18:38.827
We've evacuated 1 ,087,310 people
in under 12 hours.

838
01:18:38.992 --> 01:18:41.044
Some zones were inaccessible,

839
01:18:41.331 --> 01:18:42.884
the five high-rise targets.

840
01:18:43.042 --> 01:18:45.889
Snipers everywhere.
I have 30 casualties.

841
01:18:46.048 --> 01:18:50.140
Target number five is reported
to be packed with explosives.

842
01:18:50.348 --> 01:18:52.020
How many still haven't been evacuated?

843
01:18:52.227 --> 01:18:55.821
There's been no recent census,
but I'd guess around 1 ,000.

844
01:18:57.488 --> 01:18:58.876
That's still a lot.

845
01:18:59.033 --> 01:19:00.539
Continue the evacuation.

846
01:19:06.297 --> 01:19:07.508
- We're back-up.
- Us too.

847
01:19:20.409 --> 01:19:21.417
Dismissed.

848
01:19:33.268 --> 01:19:35.356
You put your key in the second lock.

849
01:19:35.523 --> 01:19:37.362
Then you command the launch.

850
01:19:37.527 --> 01:19:39.117
Five missiles. One per target.

851
01:19:39.280 --> 01:19:41.451
You just press the red buttons.

852
01:20:26.416 --> 01:20:28.468
To tell the truth, gentlemen...

853
01:20:28.796 --> 01:20:30.682
I'm not comfortable with this.

854
01:20:31.927 --> 01:20:33.766
May I make a comment?

855
01:20:33.931 --> 01:20:34.975
Go ahead.

856
01:20:35.101 --> 01:20:36.655
I know these vermin.

857
01:20:37.105 --> 01:20:40.237
They're the worst.
No respect for people or laws.

858
01:20:40.403 --> 01:20:43.416
They kill and rob
for the hell of it.

859
01:20:43.576 --> 01:20:46.922
It's not your fault.
They were there before you.

860
01:20:47.083 --> 01:20:50.215
How do we make vermin go away?
By talking?

861
01:20:51.049 --> 01:20:51.808
No.

862
01:20:52.009 --> 01:20:54.809
Believe me,
we have to exterminate them.

863
01:21:12.885 --> 01:21:13.562
Red alert!

864
01:21:23.949 --> 01:21:27.330
I find you frighteningly cynical.

865
01:21:27.664 --> 01:21:30.132
No, simply pragmatic.

866
01:21:30.378 --> 01:21:32.466
You promised
to improve buying power.

867
01:21:33.051 --> 01:21:36.265
It dropped
because of this parallel economy

868
01:21:36.432 --> 01:21:39.196
that deprives the state of billions.

869
01:21:39.396 --> 01:21:41.651
After this,
the gangs will take five years

870
01:21:41.818 --> 01:21:43.455
to regain their strength.

871
01:21:43.738 --> 01:21:45.245
You get breathing space

872
01:21:45.575 --> 01:21:47.711
and a second term to make a difference.

873
01:21:49.625 --> 01:21:51.547
Destroy and rebuild?

874
01:21:51.880 --> 01:21:53.267
The only solution?

875
01:21:53.717 --> 01:21:55.852
That's the way of the world.

876
01:22:10.375 --> 01:22:15.464
General, your choppers have
new-generation thermal vision?

877
01:22:15.636 --> 01:22:17.807
- That's right.
- Send them up

878
01:22:17.974 --> 01:22:19.564
to scan those buildings.

879
01:22:20.437 --> 01:22:22.358
I won't turn that key

880
01:22:22.984 --> 01:22:26.578
until I'm sure no civilian is left
in the neighbourhood.

881
01:22:27.034 --> 01:22:28.422
- Got that?
- Yes, sir.

882
01:23:05.486 --> 01:23:07.954
Trouble at the gates.
A gang's got inside.

883
01:23:08.116 --> 01:23:09.290
Capture them.

884
01:23:09.410 --> 01:23:11.082
We're trying. There's a lot of them.

885
01:23:11.582 --> 01:23:13.005
I'll take care of it.

886
01:23:18.638 --> 01:23:19.848
Check it out.

887
01:23:27.154 --> 01:23:28.745
I'll be right with you.

888
01:24:37.212 --> 01:24:39.051
We said no guns.

889
01:24:39.216 --> 01:24:42.562
No sweat. I just wanna alter
the security system.

890
01:24:47.190 --> 01:24:48.199
What's going on?

891
01:24:48.359 --> 01:24:50.779
Don't worry, it's ultra-secure here.

892
01:24:51.866 --> 01:24:53.123
Rest assured.

893
01:25:00.467 --> 01:25:01.725
He...

894
01:25:02.471 --> 01:25:03.729
is mine.

895
01:25:17.334 --> 01:25:19.173
How do you wanna play this?

896
01:25:21.008 --> 01:25:22.598
How about by the rules?

897
01:25:28.899 --> 01:25:30.489
Respect 'em from the start.

898
01:25:30.736 --> 01:25:32.290
Not when it suits you.

899
01:25:37.291 --> 01:25:39.094
I'll never share your pain.

900
01:25:39.253 --> 01:25:41.472
Mine are reinforced concrete.

901
01:25:42.718 --> 01:25:44.805
The ears and the castanets.

902
01:25:47.186 --> 01:25:48.823
Don't feel too good?

903
01:25:59.836 --> 01:26:00.595
Keep in touch.

904
01:26:00.754 --> 01:26:03.472
The five towers
have been totally evacuated.

905
01:26:06.224 --> 01:26:09.570
An hour ago,
you couldn't get people to leave.

906
01:26:10.148 --> 01:26:13.411
Maybe they finally got
the evacuation notices.

907
01:26:13.572 --> 01:26:17.203
Anyway, all five are completely empty.
You have my word.

908
01:26:24.803 --> 01:26:25.480
In that case...

909
01:26:35.240 --> 01:26:36.533
Command to Leader 1 .

910
01:26:39.875 --> 01:26:41.845
Over target in one minute.

911
01:26:42.255 --> 01:26:43.429
They're in position.

912
01:27:00.750 --> 01:27:02.672
Over there, everybody!

913
01:27:02.837 --> 01:27:06.598
This is the Command Center
of the French Army. I order you...

914
01:27:07.430 --> 01:27:10.859
And that's what you'll get
if you say another word.

915
01:27:15.780 --> 01:27:17.536
Gentlemen, I am the president.

916
01:27:18.620 --> 01:27:20.340
We've got TV y'know.

917
01:27:20.957 --> 01:27:22.298
And internet even!

918
01:27:24.088 --> 01:27:26.936
Captain Tomasso,
can you explain?

919
01:27:27.428 --> 01:27:30.109
Pictures often speak louder
than words.

920
01:27:52.687 --> 01:27:53.945
What's that?

921
01:27:54.108 --> 01:27:55.448
DISS in action.

922
01:27:55.652 --> 01:27:57.953
Killing cops to fan the flames.

923
01:27:58.157 --> 01:28:00.957
Then flatten it all
and bring in Harriburton.

924
01:28:01.372 --> 01:28:03.092
For a tasty commission.

925
01:28:04.753 --> 01:28:06.509
If pictures aren't enough...

926
01:28:07.176 --> 01:28:09.856
here's proof
of Harriburton's links to DISS.

927
01:28:10.766 --> 01:28:14.194
Your mistake was jailing me
to have a free hand.

928
01:28:15.149 --> 01:28:16.703
Should have given him leave.

929
01:28:18.239 --> 01:28:19.532
Freeze!

930
01:28:22.665 --> 01:28:23.709
Your key!

931
01:28:25.128 --> 01:28:26.338
Get your key out.

932
01:28:27.633 --> 01:28:31.513
Come on. Come on!
Get your key out.

933
01:28:32.977 --> 01:28:34.567
Put it in the lock!

934
01:28:38.029 --> 01:28:39.286
What's going on?

935
01:28:41.912 --> 01:28:43.205
Gonna be an election.

936
01:28:43.373 --> 01:28:45.959
But the fireworks come first.
Turn it.

937
01:28:47.089 --> 01:28:49.094
Tomasso!
One step and he's dead!

938
01:28:51.014 --> 01:28:52.853
Turn the key, I said!

939
01:29:03.705 --> 01:29:06.173
Signal received.
Missiles primed.

940
01:29:07.630 --> 01:29:09.516
Stop. You can't get away.

941
01:29:09.676 --> 01:29:11.894
A soldier completes his mission,

942
01:29:12.055 --> 01:29:13.858
even if it kills him.

943
01:29:14.644 --> 01:29:15.855
It's called honor.

944
01:29:16.606 --> 01:29:19.110
A concept you've never heard of

945
01:29:19.279 --> 01:29:20.785
in your ratholes.

946
01:29:21.115 --> 01:29:21.874
True.

947
01:29:22.827 --> 01:29:24.548
We prefer another concept.

948
01:29:25.040 --> 01:29:26.001
Family.

949
01:29:26.543 --> 01:29:27.836
That binds us.

950
01:29:28.004 --> 01:29:29.297
Protects us.

951
01:29:29.966 --> 01:29:31.177
Unites us.

952
01:29:31.595 --> 01:29:32.224
Yeah!

953
01:29:32.639 --> 01:29:34.145
I'll unite you!

954
01:29:34.768 --> 01:29:37.698
And kill you together!
Press the button!

955
01:29:37.941 --> 01:29:38.819
Where are you going?

956
01:29:39.318 --> 01:29:42.118
Nowhere.
I was just wondering if...

957
01:29:42.366 --> 01:29:43.707
I knew it! Cigars!

958
01:29:45.832 --> 01:29:46.876
Drop that.

959
01:29:51.676 --> 01:29:54.013
And one more for my collection.

960
01:30:14.765 --> 01:30:17.730
A real Arabian carpet,
Mr President.

961
01:30:18.314 --> 01:30:19.192
For free!

962
01:30:24.409 --> 01:30:25.287
Gentlemen...

963
01:30:28.166 --> 01:30:29.091
Miss...

964
01:30:29.252 --> 01:30:30.426
I'm sorry.

965
01:30:32.884 --> 01:30:34.605
I don't know what to say...

966
01:30:36.684 --> 01:30:39.318
Except thank you. A big thank-you.

967
01:30:40.942 --> 01:30:42.283
I owe you a lot.

968
01:30:42.780 --> 01:30:46.541
I think the nation owes you a lot.

969
01:30:48.207 --> 01:30:50.426
I know you've heard it all

970
01:30:50.712 --> 01:30:52.136
from politicians before,

971
01:30:52.298 --> 01:30:54.884
but I promise that within 48 hours,

972
01:30:55.304 --> 01:30:59.694
I'll release unprecedented funds
so your neighborhoods regain

973
01:31:00.565 --> 01:31:01.906
their dignity

974
01:31:02.360 --> 01:31:03.653
and their rightful place

975
01:31:04.072 --> 01:31:05.496
in our society.

976
01:31:08.414 --> 01:31:09.339
Thank you.

977
01:31:10.335 --> 01:31:12.589
I have a question.

978
01:31:13.174 --> 01:31:14.182
Go ahead.

979
01:31:14.301 --> 01:31:19.023
Instead of patching up
whats rotten, why not start over?

980
01:31:19.770 --> 01:31:20.565
Meaning?

981
01:31:21.106 --> 01:31:22.280
A new neighbourhood.

982
01:31:22.860 --> 01:31:24.117
A new district.

983
01:31:24.822 --> 01:31:27.076
With parks and jobs.

984
01:31:28.330 --> 01:31:29.717
I'll do it.

985
01:31:32.755 --> 01:31:35.685
You'll head up the project
until delivery.

986
01:31:38.099 --> 01:31:39.392
Yes, sir.

987
01:31:40.813 --> 01:31:43.493
You have my word
as head of government.

988
01:31:44.236 --> 01:31:45.363
And as a man?

989
01:31:47.117 --> 01:31:48.244
And as a man.

990
01:31:50.875 --> 01:31:51.800
Guys?

991
01:31:52.629 --> 01:31:53.839
Good enough for me.

992
01:31:54.006 --> 01:31:54.848
Me too.

993
01:31:55.927 --> 01:31:56.805
Solidarity.

994
01:31:57.972 --> 01:31:58.731
Clam.

995
01:31:59.683 --> 01:32:00.561
Yeah.

996
01:33:20.972 --> 01:33:23.440
That's gotta be mine.

997
01:33:29.197 --> 01:33:30.953
I'd like a little brandy.

998
01:35:55.323 --> 01:35:56.877
You know Jean Nouvel?

999
01:35:59.290 --> 01:36:01.342
He scored from me last week.

1000
01:36:02.046 --> 01:36:03.387
No, he's an architect

1001
01:36:03.716 --> 01:36:05.057
Right, an architect..
